# Line-ending and binary normalisation — approved amendment C-5.
#
# Why this file exists: the task breakdown's byte-identity assertions and
# LC-P1-10's reproducibility manifest both assume a checkout produces the same
# bytes on Windows and Linux. Without this, `git add -A` on Windows recorded
# CRLF for text files and the two platforms produced different hashes for
# identical content. That was observed in this repository: a scripted edit
# turned one markdown file entirely to CRLF and made a 25-line change appear
# as a 2088-line diff.
#
# `* text=auto eol=lf` is the load-bearing rule: git detects text vs binary,
# stores LF in the object store, and checks LF out on every platform. The
# `eol=` half is what stops Windows from converting back on checkout.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary declarations. Declared explicitly rather than left to `text=auto`
# detection so that adding a binary asset cannot silently get line-ending
# mangled by a heuristic that guessed wrong.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.whl   binary
*.tar   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.xls   binary
*.docx  binary
*.pptx  binary
*.so    binary
*.dll   binary
*.exe   binary

# Windows script exceptions — CRLF is CORRECT here, not a defect.
#
# `*.ps1` must ship CRLF: PowerShell's parser has historically mishandled
# UTF-8 without a BOM, and a `.sh` run under Git Bash on Windows needs LF.
# These two are deliberately exempt from the LF normalisation above because a
# LF .ps1 is a known source of Windows-only breakage.
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.bat   text eol=crlf

# Lockfiles are generated. Treat them as text so a CRLF checkout cannot make
# `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` or `uv lock --check` report spurious drift
# on Windows.
pnpm-lock.yaml      text eol=lf
uv.lock             text eol=lf

# Keep diffs honest for the two files that carry the project's binding
# decisions: the amendments are consumed across platforms and a line-ending
# diff would bury a real change.
docs/plans/LC-P1-01-approved-amendments.md   text eol=lf
docs/PHASE_1_WORKORDERS.md                  text eol=lf
